A||||2||BigBoyToys||Exhaust Pipe Shrouds??||||5||
Z||000000||BigBoyToys||12-02-1999||08:16 PM||||When I bought my 86GT it was missing part of the shroud that covers the exhaust pipes and the other pieces where rattling and making an aweful sound. So I pulled them all off! What kind of problems could I run into and what kind of experiences have others had while running without them? I have made sure that no wire harnesses can come in contact with the pipes and plan to remove the lower louver pieces of the hood vents eventually.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-02-1999||11:00 PM||||Those are heat shields. They protect the starter, AC compressor and hoses, and other things from radiant heat. Yes, you could cause somethings to break by removing them. It all depends on driving conditions and weather if and when such problems show up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||12-03-1999||04:40 AM||||Hopefully you didn't take the shields directly under the coil assembly, they are very important! (Unless you moved the coil.)<BR>You want to look at what is directly above the crossover pipe, namely your intake! Better off to tighten them down than to take them off, the vents will only do so much but not that much!||||reg||4
